            <div xml:id="d394">

                <pb facs="0543" n="441" xml:id="pg441"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2126/384–389.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Furniss to the Secretary of
                    State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-11-28"><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 458.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith the
                    correspondence between the Haitian Government and this legation relative to the
                    matter of blockade and closing of the ports of Aux Cayes, Jeremie, and Aquin,
                    together with copies of the official decrees and translations thereof relative
                    to the said ports.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss.</hi></signed></closer>






